	(text "STM32G474RET6 - CANopen master"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5 5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7485e92d-e4cb-4155-88c8-4e414314684b")
	)
	(text "3.3 V supply for the STM32"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.9 29.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7b06f305-504e-4924-bfbc-b881433d06c4")
	)
	(text "U18 TPS70933: 3.3 V 150 mA LDO from 5 V. Load about 55 mA (STM32 at 170 MHz\nabout 40 mA, CAN isolator logic side, LEDs). The STM32 has its own regulator,\nso it keeps running and can stop the dish when the CM5 is off or rebooting.\nR110 pulls EN to IN; ground TP37 to hold the regulator off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "23036523-1a6c-4872-bdd1-c92447f3608d")
	)
	(text "Decoupling"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.9 80.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3bfe1ce-7b4e-41a0-a49f-f606575171d8")
	)
	(text "C114-C117 one at each VDD pin (16, 32, 48, 64), C118 bulk. VBAT is on VDD.   C119/C120 at VDDA (29), C121/C122 at VREF+ (28)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 106.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0d89464b-5dc5-4489-972b-99bf3aebed0b")
	)
	(text "24 MHz crystal (HSE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.9 118.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58cc17ed-47a3-4d97-a84f-ba47f06960b4")
	)
	(text "X2 24 MHz, 12 pF load, +/-10 ppm:\nCANopen bit timing needs a crystal.\nC112/C113 15 pF (same crystal and\ncaps as the USB hub of the CM4 board)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99 139 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "152446c6-ccc4-4584-a6be-429ecfd1ade0")
	)
	(text "Reset and boot control from the CM5"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.9 158.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58031963-5998-48f2-a63d-87febdbdb4ef")
	)
	(text "MCU_RST (CM5 GPIO23) high turns Q7 on and holds the\nSTM32 in reset. R123 keeps Q7 off while the CM5 is off\nor booting (GPIO23 also defaults to pull-down).\nMCU_BOOT0 (CM5 GPIO24) high at reset starts the STM32\nsystem bootloader, which listens on USART1 (PA9/PA10),\nthe same UART the CM5 uses: the CM5 can reflash the\nSTM32 with no SWD probe. R125 keeps BOOT0 low.\nKeep PB8 an input in firmware: it must never drive the\nCM5 pin while the CM5 is off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 84 183 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0b424232-adbc-4a23-9b57-22bcb5f312d4")
	)
	(text "UART to the CM5 (USART1), buffered against back-powering"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 255.5 29.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4458d163-3e91-4c7e-a2e7-47a2bbadca52")
	)
	(text "Same scheme as the RoboClaw link of the CM4 board.\nU16 and U19 run from 3V3_CM5. With the CM5 off their\noutputs are high-Z and their inputs tolerate 3.3 V\n(74LVC Ioff), so the STM32 never drives a CM5 pin\n(CM5 datasheet 4.2.1: no voltage on any pin of an\nunpowered module).\nR126 holds the line idle-high while the STM32 is in\nreset; R127 holds MCU_RX idle-high while the CM5 is off.\nCM5 side: GPIO12 = TX, GPIO13 = RX (UART4 on the CM5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345 36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8f423861-d11c-48f8-b2d6-fabc1e767dc1")
	)
	(text "SWD + virtual COM (STDC14)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 255.5 108.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e3bfc762-158a-422b-9fcb-e8382aaf3d34")
	)
	(text "ST STDC14 pinout (STLINK-V3). VCP: pin 13 = target RX (PA3), pin 14 = target TX (PA2), USART2 / LPUART1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 256.54 148.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67535143-4b20-419f-b070-6667a125dd22")
	)
	(text "CANopen status LEDs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 346.94 108.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3d3c0cf6-2d8a-4dc6-82c6-1d6d829e2d51")
	)
	(text "Isolated CAN transceiver, bus filter, termination and RJ45"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 264.16 162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "14473577-58b8-4f36-a05c-ed4591e8b802")
	)
	(text "Role: the STM32 is the CANopen master. It runs the position / velocity loop: it commands the velocity of the servo drives over CAN and reads their\nposition back over CAN. The CM5 sends it pointing commands over the UART, as it did to the RoboClaw.\n\nPin use:\n- PA9 = USART1_TX to CM5 GPIO13, PA10 = USART1_RX from CM5 GPIO12. USART1 is also a system-bootloader UART.\n- PA12 = FDCAN1_TX, PA11 = FDCAN1_RX (AF9).\n- PA13 = SWDIO, PA14 = SWCLK, PB3 = SWO. PA2 / PA3 = debug UART on the STDC14 virtual COM port.\n- PC6 = LED_RUN (green), PC7 = LED_ERR (red): CANopen indicator LEDs (CiA 303-3), active high.\n- PF0 / PF1 = 24 MHz HSE, PG10 = NRST, PB8 = BOOT0.\nAll other pins are unused and left open (no-connect flags). Set them to analog mode in firmware.\nThere is no encoder or limit-switch interface on this board: those are separate CANopen nodes on the same bus (future boards)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 226.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "32ac9a17-21c3-4d8b-a6a1-3237aae51b74")
	)
